  "label": "User projected onto the shocked woman visual",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the shocked woman, as her exaggerated expression and gesture are used to represent the user's own perceived shock or disbelief in response to the false biblical claim presented in the text. The meme uses this visual trope to make the user feel as if they are experiencing the shock value of the misinformation, thereby amplifying the emotional impact and encouraging engagement with the harmful message.",
